## Conventions for OpenCode delegations

This file is loaded automatically by OpenCode (`opencode run`) when it operates in this
project directory. The conventions here apply equally to delegated work.

### General

- Read existing files before creating new ones. Match their style.
- Do not introduce new dependencies without an explicit instruction.
- Do not edit `package.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `pyproject.toml`, lockfiles, or CI configs
  unless the spec explicitly requests it.
- Do not invent APIs. Grep the codebase before calling a function you "think" exists.

### Code style

- (Project-specific: fill in your own naming rules, error handling, import order.)

### Tests

- New code requires tests in the same commit.
- Run the acceptance test listed in the spec before finishing.
- Do not modify existing tests unless the spec asks for it.

### Documentation

- Docstrings: (project-specific format)
- Inline comments: only where the *why* is non-obvious. Never explain *what*.

### Forbidden actions

- `git commit`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`, `git checkout --` — never call these.
  The orchestrator decides when to commit.
- `rm -rf`, `curl ... | sh`, `sudo` — never run.
- Network calls to external services — denied by permission policy.
